# Line endings are pinned to LF everywhere, on purpose.
#
# This is a correctness requirement, not a style preference. Ground-truth label sets
# carry a SHA-256 of the corpus file they describe, and refuse to score if it does not
# match. If Git rewrote line endings on checkout, a fresh clone on Windows would produce
# different bytes, every hash check would fail, and the answer keys would appear to have
# drifted from code nobody had touched.
#
# The same applies to corpus/dictionary.json and the requirements hashes.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artefacts must never be line-ending converted.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.svg binary
